            <div xml:id="d632">

                <pb facs="0918" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.311F1/166: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-07-28T13:00:00+01:00">July 28, 1933—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 28—7:38 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>226. For Wallace from Morgenthau. “Replying to your 209, July 27, 4 p.m., at
                    yesterday’s meeting differences arose between Canada and some of the Europeans
                    which proved irreconcilable. We recessed until August 21 at London. Morgenthau
                    personally believes now that no satisfactory agreement can be reached within
                    reasonable time, if at all, and advises your announcing your plan immediately.
                    Morgenthau sails on <hi rendition="#italic">Berengaria</hi> Saturday and will
                    report Washington on arrival. Will cable further details. Murphy agrees with
                    Morgenthau’s conclusions but will try to get Bennett’s reaction yesterday’s
                    meeting.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
